IR_FINDINGS = 'IRAN (IR): research notes for cl-stack-calendars#44.\n\nSOURCES. The official calendar authority is the Calendar Center (مرکز تقویم) of the Institute of Geophysics, University of Tehran.\ncalendar.ut.ac.ir answers curl with an ArvanCloud JavaScript challenge, so every Calendar Center file was taken from the Wayback Machine (id_ raw copies).\nCached under ~/.cache/cl-stack-calendars/ir/ut/: holiday-1378..1404.pdf (no 1381 list exists, so Full-1381.pdf, the full official calendar, is used),\nfull-1399.pdf, and Kabise_Shamsi_1206-1498.pdf. time.ir is reachable directly: timeir/event-year.html (1405) and Wayback snapshots timeir/wb_*.html.\nThe CDX listings are cdx_ut*.txt. The 1405 PDF (Calendar-1405.pdf) is archived only as challenge pages, so time.ir (publisher of the Calendar Center calendar) stands in for 1405.\n\nNOWRUZ RULE. 1 Farvardin is the day of the March equinox if it occurs before noon Iran standard time (UTC+03:30, meridian 52.5 E), otherwise the next day.\nThat is the Calendar Center practice; the statute (قانون تقویم, 11 Farvardin 1304) was not fetched. Equinox moments seen: 1381 cover page 1380-12-29 22:46:02 -> 1 Farvardin = 2002-03-21; 1404 time.ir 12:31:30 on 2025-03-20 -> 2025-03-21.\nOFFICIAL TABLE PROBLEM: the Kabise 1206-1498 table\'s date column (headed "1 Farvardin") is inconsistent with its own leap stars\n(1399* yet 1400 -> 20 March 2021; the real date was 21 March 2021, a Sunday, as Holiday-1400 confirms). That column matches the Tehran date of the equinox, so it is kept separately (IR_NOWRUZ_TABLE_COLUMN).\nIR_NOWRUZ 1379-1405 is read from the yearly official calendars (weekday of 1 Farvardin in every list; Gregorian printed in Full-1381 and time.ir 1405).\nIR_NOWRUZ 1406-1420 is chained from the official leap stars (1408 is a 5-year leap). Every value is the column date or the next day.\n\nHOLIDAY LIST BY ERA (from the yearly lists; statutes in IR_STATUTES):\n- 2000 (1378/1379) on: Nowruz 1-4 Farvardin, 12 and 13 Farvardin, 14 and 15 Khordad, 22 Bahman, 29 Esfand; lunar 9/10 Muharram, 20/28/last Safar, 17 Rabi I, 3 Jumada II (from 1379; added by amend-1378), 13/27 Rajab, 15 Shaban, 21 Ramadan, 1 Shawwal, 25 Shawwal, 10/18 Dhu al-Hijja.\n- 2 Shawwal: law of 1390-06-06/08. In force for Eid 1432, so 2011-09-01 is added although Holiday-1390 (printed earlier) lacks it. Listed from Holiday-1391 on.\n- 8 Rabi al-Awwal (Imam Hasan Askari): Law on Permanent Provisions of the Development Plans, Art. 37(h), approved 1395-11-10, gazette 1396-01-16. In lists from 1396 (first 2017-11-26).\n- 29 Esfand: the consolidated 1359 text (Art. 3, added 1378) says its holiday is cancelled, but every official list keeps it. Lists followed; disagreement noted. Statute history not resolved (rc.majlis.ir unreachable).\n- 30 Esfand in leap years: python-holidays and time.ir (1399, 1403 snapshots) mark it "آخرین روز سال". The Calendar Center lists and the full official calendar 1399 do not, so it is excluded and listed in IR_ADHOC. Open question.\n- Ad-hoc (Art. 2 of the 1359 law, Council of Ministers): 2026-03-01..07 (7-day closure after the Leader\'s death; offices reopened 17 Esfand = 2026-03-08) and 2026-07-05/06 (funeral, nationwide). Both are included in IR_YEARS[2026].days; the sources are secondary news reports of cabinet decisions. 2023-08-02/03 heat closure is in IR_ADHOC only (python-holidays says 08-01/02; DW: Wed-Thu = 08-02/03).\n\nLUNAR DATES / CHANGES AFTER SIGHTING. The yearly lists are forecasts. Checks made:\n(a) Full-1381 (corrected edition) footnote: Ramadan 1423 began one day later than computed, per the official announcement. The corrected dates (21 Ramadan 2002-11-26, Eid 2002-12-06) are used. The original forecast list is not archived, so nothing goes in suppressed.\n(b) Every lunar holiday 2001-2026 was compared with python-holidays 0.109, whose Iranian dates are "confirmed" 2001-2026 (a secondary source, apparently from time.ir).\nAll agree except: 2000 Tasua/Ashura (cal 04-14/15 vs ph 04-15/16) and 2000 Eid al-Fitr (cal 12-27 vs ph 12-28); ph marks 2000 as estimated, so the calendar is kept.\n2011 21 Ramadan: cal 08-22 vs ph 08-21. Calendar kept, because Ramadan 1432 began Tuesday 2011-08-02 per the Leader\'s office committee (Hamshahri, 1390-05-11).\nAnd 2002 (ph lacks the 1381 correction).\nNo other announced changes were found, so suppressed lists are empty. Eid al-Fitr 1446 (2025-03-31) and 1444 (2023-04-22) matched the calendar.\n(c) Two coincidences not printed separately are added as second names: 2006-03-21 Arbaeen on Nowruz, and 2019-03-20 13 Rajab on 29 Esfand.\nTRANSCRIPTION ERRATA in the official lists: Holiday-1380 Tasua/Ashura day numbers (16/17 Farvardin printed, 15/16 meant: weekdays and lunar arithmetic agree), and Holiday-1383 Tasua/Ashura weekday labels (solar dates kept).\n\nCOVERAGE. 2000-2026: primary (Calendar Center lists; 2026-03-21 on from time.ir). 2027: secondary/partial, only 01-01..03-20 (time.ir 1405); the 1406 calendar was not reachable.\nStatute texts are secondary reproductions (shenasname.ir, edalatsara, news); the official Majlis database (rc.majlis.ir) and the gazette were unreachable.\nPrimary Iranian news agencies (irna.ir, leader.ir, khamenei.ir) return bot walls or 403.\n'


